  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-for-spec-authors\r\n\r\n> Do any synchronous setup work, while still on the event loop\\.\r\n\r\nThis new #event-loop-for-spec-authors section, while helpful, does not explain how one's algorithms end up on the (relevant) event loop.  It seems from grovelling thru the specs (HTML, Infra, Writing Promise-Using Specs aka [promises guide](https://www.w3.org/2001/tag/doc/promises-guide/)) that one's algorithms start out by default on the event loop (main thread) unless explicitly stated otherwise. Is this correct?  Perhaps this #event-loop-for-spec-authors section should explain this more clearly, perhaps also in [promises guide](https://www.w3.org/2001/tag/doc/promises-guide/)\r\n\r\nPerhaps [promises guide](https://www.w3.org/2001/tag/doc/promises-guide/) ought to reference [#event-loop-for-spec-authors ](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-for-spec-authors), and vice-versa. ",
